Let's define the sets, parameters, and variables:

Sets:
T = {purchase and payment, query and refund}

Parameters:
p_{purchase and payment} = 5 \\\\text{ minutes}
p_{query and refund} = 3 \\\\text{ minutes}
c_{purchase and payment} = 10 \\\\text{ dollars}
c_{query and refund} = 5 \\\\text{ dollars}
max_{purchase and payment} = 60 \\\\text{ tasks/hour}
max_{query and refund} = 80 \\\\text{ tasks/hour}

Variables:
x_{purchase and payment} \\\\geq 0, \\\\text{ integer: number of purchase and payment tasks processed per hour}
x_{query and refund} \\\\geq 0, \\\\text{ integer: number of query and refund tasks processed per hour}

Objective:
\\\\min \\\\left( 10 x_{purchase and payment} + 5 x_{query and refund} \\\\right)

Constraints:
5 x_{purchase and payment} \\\\leq 60 \\\\quad \\\\text{(processing time constraint for purchases)}
3 x_{query and refund} \\\\leq 80 \\\\quad \\\\text{(processing time constraint for queries)}

Solve:
Using a solver, we obtain the optimal solution:
x_{purchase and payment} = 12 \\\\text{ tasks/hour}
x_{query and refund} = 26 \\\\text{ tasks/hour}

Total cost:
10 \\\\times 12 + 5 \\\\times 26 = 120 + 130 = 250 \\\\text{ dollars/hour}

